# ROMANIAN DEADLIFT

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Romanian Deadlift (RDL) is a bilateral hip-hinge exercise designed to develop posterior chain strength through controlled eccentric and concentric loading.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the primary exercises for improving hip extension strength, eccentric hamstring capacity and posterior chain robustness.

---

# Philosophy

The Romanian Deadlift is not a maximal lifting exercise.

It is a movement-quality exercise emphasizing controlled force production and posterior chain development.

CAS selects the Romanian Deadlift when improving hip-dominant force production, injury resilience and movement efficiency.

